# pins.env -- version pin for the sandbox provisioning wrappers.
#
# This file is the ONLY moving part of the sandbox/ tree (see
# docs/design/PROVISION.DESIGN.md, "Sandbox wrapper tree"). All behavioral
# churn lives inside clai, behind this pin: rolling out new provisioning
# behavior to every provider = editing this file in ONE reviewed change
# (the pin bump is the review gate, per the supply-chain stance documented
# in .claude/hooks/session-start.sh and ai-tools issue #72).
#
# Sourced (and exported) by sandbox/provision.sh, and read as a --pins file by
# `lmde acquire` (keys CLAI_VERSION + AST_MCP_VERSION + SKILLS_VERSION +
# ADMIN_VERSION; acquire also carries a git-mirror row, unpinned here --
# see issue #188). Plain KEY="value"
# assignments only -- no logic, no command substitution. `lmde acquire` NEVER
# edits this file; it only reads it.
#
# CLAI_VERSION gates the clai LAUNCHER only. The #145 model (skills + MCP
# catalog riding inside the clai wheel, CLAI_VERSION as their content-stamp
# gate) is REVERSED by LMDE.DESIGN.md section 2 (2026-07-30):
# skills + the catalog now ship as the standalone @nine-at-a-time-media/skills
# DATA package, published by template-tools CI on merge and acquired floating
# by default (SKILLS_VERSION below). A skill edit reaches sandboxes on the
# merge that lands it -- the review gate is the PR into protected main.
#
# With NO --pins, `lmde acquire` floats EVERY package to registry latest; the
# sandbox always passes --pins THIS file so the review gate applies. An UNSET
# key here means "float THAT package to latest" (loud-but-open, same as
# CLAI_VERSION below) -- a half-populated file pins one and floats the other by
# that rule, never by accident.
#
# Delivery transport (RD1, #101): clai is installed from GitHub Packages
# (npm.pkg.github.com) as @nine-at-a-time-media/clai, NOT fetched as a
# GitHub Release wheel over api.github.com -- that path is blocked by the
# Claude web agent proxy. The old CLAI_SHA256 wheel-digest pin is retired
# (RD3): npm verifies every downloaded tarball against the registry's
# published integrity hash, and a published version on GitHub Packages is
# immutable -- so the supply-chain gate is the pinned VERSION plus npm's
# built-in integrity check. The #72 stance is intact: a default-branch
# push still does not grant execution in a consumer, because consumers
# install the pinned released version.
#
# To bump the pin: set CLAI_VERSION to a released, published version of
# @nine-at-a-time-media/clai (`npm view @nine-at-a-time-media/clai version
# --registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com` reports the latest -- the explicit
# registry is required, else npm queries registry.npmjs.org and fails for
# this private scoped package; a classic read:packages token must be
# configured for the scope). If it is ever reset to UNSET, provision.sh
# fails LOUDLY-but-open: it logs the fill-in procedure and exits 0 so
# sessions still start.

# clai (executable code: pinned version, npm registry integrity). Session
# hook scripts ship INSIDE this package (installed by `clai hooks
# install`), so they roll out via the same CLAI_VERSION bump -- no
# separate hooks pin.
# Current pin: @nine-at-a-time-media/clai@0.7.0 (published on GitHub
# Packages; an npm wrapper around clai's self-contained shiv .pyz).
#
# 0.7.0 (template-tools#253, PR #254) labels the tmux window with the agent
# name for the duration of a launch, restoring the window's prior name and
# automatic-rename state on exit. Before it, every clai window read
# `python3.12`: clai waits on the agent rather than exec-ing it (post-hooks
# need clai's process to outlive the agent), so clai is what tmux's
# automatic-rename sees, and claude/gemini/codex were indistinguishable in the
# window list. tmux only; `CLAI_NO_WINDOW_LABEL=1` opts out; outside tmux no
# tmux subprocess is spawned. No provisioning behavior changed, so this bump
# carries no skills or catalog delta -- it is a pure launcher improvement.
#
# 0.6.0 (template-tools#145, #164) is the FIRST release carrying the
# bundled-data contract: the skills tree + MCP catalog ride INSIDE the wheel
# as clai/_data (content-stamped at clai/_data/SOURCE_STAMP), so `clai
# provision` materializes them fully offline -- no cross-repo clone. (That
# content-stamp gate role is SUPERSEDED by Revision 1 -- see the header note
# and SKILLS_VERSION below; clai/_data survives only as clai's bootstrap
# fallback.)
#
# Floor (do NOT pin below 0.5.5): 0.5.5 (template-tools#144) is the first
# release whose MCP generator honors RD5 -- the canonical manifest names
# ${HOME}/.local/bin/ast-mcp, emitted LITERAL into the committed .mcp.json
# (Claude expands it in the spawned server's process) and RESOLVED to an
# absolute path in the user-scope codex/agy/opencode configs (those clients do
# not expand variables). Every earlier clai rewrote .mcp.json back to the
# unexpandable ${AST_MCP_BIN} on every provision run, so pinning below 0.5.5
# reintroduces that regression.
# 0.8.0 (tds-utils#190) is the first release carrying the package-first
# source order (clai provision prefers the acquired skills payload over the
# wheel's bundled _data fallback -- LMDE.DESIGN.md section 2).
# NOTE: goes live when the clai-v0.8.0 tag is pushed on template-tools main
# (proxy denies tag pushes from sandboxes; manual step). Until then acquire
# degrades fail-open, keeping the installed clai with a loud warning.
# Matches the fleet pin in template-tools packages/skills/pins.env; this
# copy serves only the unmigrated providers and the transition fallback
# (SANDBOX-LIFECYCLE.DESIGN.md D1).
CLAI_VERSION="0.8.0"

# ast-mcp (executable MCP server: pinned version, npm registry integrity).
# Installed by `lmde acquire` at ~/.local/bin/ast-mcp from GitHub Packages as
# @nine-at-a-time-media/ast-mcp. Same UNSET/loud-but-open convention as
# CLAI_VERSION: a real value pins that exact version; UNSET (or an absent key)
# floats ast-mcp to registry latest. Pinning both here through one --pins file
# is what gates the whole tooling surface in ONE reviewed change.
#
# Now a REAL pin (was "latest"): floating left the second half of the tooling
# surface ungated, contradicting this file's one-file-gating stance, and
# tds-utils#120's "skip provision when the installed version already matches
# the intended pin" needs a concrete intended version to compare against.
# 0.4.0 is the current published latest (2026-08-13; the frozen 0.3.x pins
# were the #194 staleness class).
# To bump: `npm view @nine-at-a-time-media/ast-mcp version
# --registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com` (with a classic read:packages token
# configured) reports the latest published version; set it and land via PR.
AST_MCP_VERSION="0.4.0"

# skills (@nine-at-a-time-media/skills: INERT DATA -- the canonical skills
# tree + MCP catalog, no binary). Deliberately UNSET: floating to registry
# latest IS the design intent (LMDE.DESIGN.md section 2) --
# every fresh session starts with the current skills, no human rollout step.
# The package is published automatically by template-tools CI on merge to
# main, so the review gate is that PR, not this pin. Set a concrete version
# here ONLY to freeze skills in an emergency (a bad skill merge); remove the
# freeze once the fix lands upstream.
SKILLS_VERSION="UNSET"

# gadmin (executable code: pinned version, npm registry integrity). Installed
# by `lmde acquire` at ~/.local/bin/gadmin from GitHub Packages as
# @nine-at-a-time-media/admin -- the npm name is `admin`, the binary it ships
# is `gadmin`. Same UNSET/loud-but-open convention as the pins above.
#
# Why it is on the rail at all (tds-utils#186): the github-workflow skill ranks
# `gadmin` ahead of the GitHub MCP tools on token cost, and ships a zero-
# dependency `gadmin github-gitapi` tier built specifically for sandboxes
# (native fetch + $GITHUB_TOKEN). Before this key existed, acquire never
# installed the package, so every cloud sandbox had neither `gadmin` nor `gh`
# and fell back to the MCP tier the skill rates at ~5-10x the tokens.
#
# 0.4.0 is the version declared by packages/naatm-admin/package.json on
# template-tools' default branch. Confirm it is actually PUBLISHED before
# relying on it -- `npm view @nine-at-a-time-media/admin version
# --registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com` (classic read:packages token
# required). A pin ahead of the published latest degrades fail-open: acquire
# warns and keeps whatever is installed, it does not break the session.
ADMIN_VERSION="0.4.0"

# Canonical source repo (stable; not a pin). Skills + the MCP catalog ship
# as the @nine-at-a-time-media/skills package (SKILLS_VERSION above,
# Revision 1) -- they never float to a repo default branch and no longer
# ride the clai release either. TEMPLATE_TOOLS_REPO/AI_TOOLS_REPO are
# retained only for the not-yet-migrated bootstrap-and-fetch providers and are
# slated for cleanup once every provider is on acquire-then-configure.
TEMPLATE_TOOLS_REPO="nine-at-a-time-media/template-tools"
AI_TOOLS_REPO="nine-at-a-time-media/template-tools"
